{"Two class methods with the same name are defined for downsizing, and in Ruby the latter definition overrides the former, so calls that pass width, height, and options now either raise an ArgumentError for wrong number of arguments or are interpreted with the wrong parameters": 0.9560676217079163, "Client-side upload validation uses a hardcoded 10MB limit instead of the configured per-type site settings, which can either block uploads that the server would accept or allow uploads that the server will reject, and reports an incorrect maximum size to the user": 0.9897081851959229, "Using rescue nil on the download call means tempfile can be nil when the download fails, but later code unconditionally calls tempfile.size when building the upload, which will raise a NoMethodError at runtime instead of cleanly surfacing a validation or download error": 0.5459195971488953}